method.description:
A [NetwAction] for an action such as firing or placing something, bound to [param authority] the server runs to judge it.
Repeated calls return the same [NetwAction].
[codeblock]
@onready var place_bomb := Netw.action(_place_bomb)

func _ready() -> void:
    place_bomb.predict = _show_bomb_now

func _place_bomb(ctx: NetwActionContext) -> void:
    var bomb := BOMB.instantiate()
    ctx.bind(bomb)
    bombs.add_child(bomb)
[/codeblock]
The server judges an action before other peers see it. To let a client spawn, move and despawn a node first and have the server confirm it later, see [member NetwEntity.lifecycle].

Declares extra configuration for [param callable] that [annotation @GDScript.@rpc] does not cover.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_rpc(self.aim).controller().quantize(
            NetwQuantizeAngle.new().bits(12).centered(),
    )

@rpc("any_peer", "unreliable")
func aim(yaw: float) -> void:
    turret.rotation.y = yaw
[/codeblock]

Lets clients request a scene change. [param handler] runs on the server for every request and returns [constant @GlobalScope.OK] to allow it.
[codeblock]
func _init() -> void:
    Netw.configure_scene_requests(authorize_scene_request)

func authorize_scene_request(
    player: NetwPlayer,
    destination: String,
    scope: Netw.SceneChange
) -> Error:
    if scope != Netw.SCENE_CHANGE_PLAYER:
        return ERR_UNAUTHORIZED
    return OK if unlocked(player, destination) else ERR_UNAUTHORIZED
[/codeblock]

The [NetwConnectHandle] of the [member Node.multiplayer], used to connect to other peers and probe servers.
[codeblock]
var c := Netw.connection(self)
var ticket := c.create_peer(
        ENetMultiplayerPeer,
        NetwMultiplayer.TRANSPORT_MODE_HOST,
        "", {port = 21253}, _created)

func _created(peer: MultiplayerPeer, error: Error, detail: String):
    if error == OK:
        Netw.of(self).multiplayer_peer = peer
[/codeblock]
This is optional. Assigning a [MultiplayerPeer] to [member MultiplayerAPI.multiplayer_peer] works as usual.

Returns a copy of the state of [param entity] at [param tick]. It is empty when nothing was recorded.
[codeblock]
func _place_bomb(ctx: NetwActionContext, pos: Vector2) -> void:
    var past := Netw.sample(entity, ctx.view_tick)
    if not past.has_value(&"position"):
        ctx.deny()
        return
[/codeblock]

Returns the table of the schema [param name] from [method configure_schema].
[codeblock]
@onready var mobs := Netw.table(self, &"Mob")

func _ready() -> void:
    mobs.received.connect(_on_mobs)
[/codeblock]
